    "final_answer": "Based on the config file `config/lamp.toml`, the lamp has:\n\n- **range_nm = 18** - This specifies a spectral bandwidth of 18 nanometers\n\nThis typically refers to the **Full Width at Half Maximum (FWHM)** of the lamp's emission spectrum, meaning the lamp emits light across a wavelength range of approximately 18 nm. This is relatively narrow and suggests:\n\n- Could be an LED lamp with narrow spectral output\n- Or a laser diode with precise wavelength control\n- The actual center wavelength would depend on other configuration parameters not shown in this file\n\nThe 18 nm range indicates good spectral purity, which is important for applications requiring specific wavelengths (like spectroscopy, fluorescence excitation, or color-critical lighting)."
